ities this approach also help  you avoid unexpect  and unwanted uneven behavior of your  application where some parts work you  know very very well maybe more well than  you need them and other parts and  disappoint your users because they don't  work as well as it's required so let's  talk about how to define this process  right in Google terms we use something  called SL ice or service level  indicators as a way of measuring the  end-to-end availability of a  particularly user activity and we use  SLO S or service level objectives as a  term to describe the expectation for how  those SLI is emerging practice for our  users right and so if you end up with SL  is that accurately measure your users  activities and SL owes that numerically  describe what those SLI should be in a  well running system you have something  very useful which is a set of  measurements that are machine measurable  right so you can actually measure them  constantly record them go back and look  at them later alert on them when they  aren't working the way you want and they  also allow you to tie the behavior of  your system to specific systems specific  components and specific development  teams who are working on the system and  that in turn allows you to manage your  development and deployment process and  it allows you to make decisions about  how we run your service on a cloud so if  that's all a very abstract concept let's  talk about this in practice and I'll use  obviously and it made up example here  but one that we can mostly relate to so  suppose I'm doing an assessment for a  banking application and as you can see  on this slide I've listed the business  goals in priority order right we have  several user activities and those  activities map to business goals right  for each of those goals I've mapped out  the relevant user activities in my  application and I can see that really my  top goal is to retain the customers that  I've got and I know that in order to do  that I need to be